# PodMind — Complete Implementation Walkthrough

> [!TIP]
> The PodMind platform is now fully implemented! This document outlines the completed architecture and provides instructions on how to launch the system.

## Architectural Summary

PodMind is an AI-driven Kubernetes observability platform that utilizes a multi-agent framework to discover root causes, build causal dependency graphs, and provide LLM-powered recommendations.

The system is broken down into three core tiers:
1. **Data Collection Pipeline (Python/APScheduler)**: Pulls metrics from the K8s API, Prometheus, and Kubelet, normalizing them and pushing them into Redis TimeSeries and Streams.
2. **AI Intelligence Layer (Python/FastAPI)**: Runs a LangGraph DAG every 30 seconds orchestrating specialized agents (CPU, Memory, Network, Storage) and a Granger-causality Dependency Mapper. It uses Anthropic Claude / OpenAI GPT-4o (with local Ollama fallback) to synthesize the findings.
3. **React Dashboard (Vite/TypeScript)**: A highly dynamic, glassmorphic UI utilizing D3.js to visualize the causal dependency graph and a real-time WebSocket connection to display new AI insights instantly.

