## How to Run the Platform

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Make sure Docker is running on your machine before executing these steps.

**1. Start the Kubernetes Cluster & Infrastructure**
Open a terminal in the project root (`ABB/`) and run:
```bash
bash cluster/setup.sh
```
This will start Minikube, deploy the Prometheus stack, and install the Redis TimeSeries database.

**2. Deploy the Demo Workloads**
Inject the stress workloads (CPU burn, memory leak, PVC saturation, network flood) to give the AI something to analyze:
```bash
kubectl apply -f cluster/demo-workloads/
```

**3. Start the Backend API & Collector**
Open a new terminal and run:
```bash
# Start the backend server (FastAPI)
python -m api.main

# In another terminal, start the metric collector
python -m collector.main
```

**4. Start the React Dashboard**
Open a new terminal, navigate to the dashboard directory, and start Vite:
```bash
cd dashboard
npm run dev
```

Visit `http://localhost:5173` in your browser. You will see the PodMind dashboard waiting for the first 30-second analysis cycle to complete. Once the AI generates its first insight, the UI will automatically update via WebSockets to show the Granger causality graph and root cause analysis!
